- vendor/demo_common/, vendor/web-shared/, and vendor/skills/ are carried from that
  repository. Copyright 2026 Anthropic PBC. Three lines differ from the pinned commit:
    - vendor/demo_common/merchant.py declares its listing route as {listing_id:path},
      because a Shopify product id is a gid with slashes in it. That is the merchant
      counterpart of the /api/products/{product_id:path} route the carried copy
      already has.
    - vendor/demo_common/merchant.py and vendor/demo_common/storefront.py build the
      .env path in the authentication error message without an examples/ prefix. The
      blueprint keeps its examples under examples/ and this repository keeps them at
      the root, so the message reads merchant/.env and storefront/.env, which is where
      those files are.
  All three stand until the pinned commit carries equivalent fixes.
- The blueprint's core packages (commerce-common, shopping-agent, merchant-agent)
  are not part of this repository; requirements.txt installs them from Anthropic's
  repository at a pinned commit.
